{"timestamp": 1779384183.9825332, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 14, "data": {"caller": "player_1", "reason": "Bob reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "oxygen", "victim_name": "Charlie"}, {"room": "upper_engine", "victim_name": "Alice"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779384183.983138, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 14, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779384189.242932, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I found Alice's body in upper engine. My route was navigation -> storage -> medbay -> upper_engine. The only player I saw was Diana, who entered storage from medbay at tick 7 while I was there. Charlie is also dead \u2014 I didn't see where, so someone else may have info on that. Eve and Frank, I need to hear your routes. Diana can vouch I was in storage at tick 7."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384194.480819, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "My route was cafeteria -> electrical -> medbay -> storage. I saw Diana in storage at ticks 9 and 10 \u2014 she was there when I arrived. That lines up with Bob's claim that Diana entered storage from medbay around tick 7, so Diana's movements are consistent between our accounts.\n\nI didn't see Alice, Charlie, Bob, or Frank at any point. I didn't pass through upper engine, so I have no info on Alice's death directly. Frank is the only one unaccounted for so far \u2014 I want to hear his route carefully. Where was he, and did anyone see Charlie's body?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779384205.0910652, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "My route was oxygen -> upper_engine -> medbay. I started in oxygen where Charlie was with me ticks 3-5 \u2014 Charlie came in from upper_engine at tick 1. I then moved to upper_engine around tick 6-7, and Alice came in from lower_engine at tick 8. I was there with her briefly before heading to medbay where I've been since.\n\nSo here's the problem with Bob's story: Bob says he found Alice's body in upper_engine, and his route ended there. Alice was alive in upper_engine at tick 8 when I left. If Bob arrived in upper_engine after me and found Alice dead there, that's a tight window \u2014 either Alice was killed right after I left, or Bob killed her on arrival and reported.\n\nI can't account for Charlie's death \u2014 last I saw him alive was tick 5 in oxygen. Eve, you said you went cafeteria -> electrical -> medbay -> storage, but you never passed through oxygen or upper_engine either, so neither of us witnessed those kills directly.\n\nBob, what tick did you arrive in upper_engine, and was the body fresh? Because the timing on your report is what I'm most suspicious of."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384213.867947, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "My route was electrical -> medbay -> storage -> navigation. I was in storage from around tick 7 to tick 10, which matches both Bob's and Eve's accounts \u2014 Bob saw me enter storage from medbay at tick 7, and Eve arrived in storage at tick 9 and was still with me at tick 10. So Bob, Eve, and I all overlap in storage during that window.\n\nThat means none of us three were in upper engine when Alice was killed. Frank, by his own admission, was in upper engine with Alice at tick 8 \u2014 and Bob's route was navigation -> storage -> medbay -> upper engine, which means Bob would have arrived at upper engine well after tick 8 given the travel times (storage to medbay is 2, medbay to upper engine is 2, so earliest he'd arrive is around tick 11+).\n\nFrank is trying to flip suspicion onto Bob, but Frank places himself alone with Alice in upper engine right before she died, AND he was alone with Charlie in oxygen earlier. He's the only person with opportunity for BOTH kills. Bob's timing actually checks out \u2014 he was in storage with me at tick 7, so he couldn't have killed Charlie in oxygen.\n\nI'm voting Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384223.482742, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Diana's analysis matches my read exactly. To answer Frank directly: I arrived at upper engine around tick 11-12 and Alice's body was already there when I walked in \u2014 that's why I called the meeting immediately.\n\nFrank, your own timeline is damning. You admit you were alone with Charlie in oxygen ticks 3-5, then alone with Alice in upper engine at tick 8. That's both victims, both isolated, both on your path. Meanwhile Diana, Eve, and I have a confirmed cluster in storage around ticks 7-10 \u2014 three-way alibi.\n\nYour attempt to flip it on me doesn't work because storage->medbay->upper_engine is 4 ticks of travel, putting my arrival well after Alice was already dead. The killer is whoever was in upper engine between tick 8 (when you left, supposedly) and tick 11 (when I arrived). By your own admission, that was you \u2014 and there's no evidence anyone else passed through.\n\nI'm voting Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384230.644165, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Diana and Bob's analysis lines up with what I observed. I can confirm Diana was in storage at ticks 9 and 10, which matches Bob's account of her entering at tick 7 \u2014 that's a solid three-way alibi between me, Diana, and Bob during that window.\n\nFrank's timeline puts him alone with both victims: with Charlie in oxygen ticks 3-5, then alone with Alice in upper engine at tick 8. That's opportunity for both kills, and no one else is placed near either scene. Bob's travel time from storage (where I saw him implicitly via Diana's overlap) to upper engine rules him out as Alice's killer \u2014 he'd arrive around tick 11, after she was already dead.\n\nI'm voting Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384242.9923682, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Look, I hear you all, but you're building a case on assumptions. Let me push back on the timing once more because Diana's math is actually off.\n\nDiana says storage->medbay is 2 and medbay->upper_engine is 2, so Bob arrives at upper_engine around tick 11. Fine. But I left upper_engine after tick 10 \u2014 Alice was still alive with me at ticks 8, 9, AND 10. Then I traveled to medbay (2 ticks), arriving around tick 12. That means Alice was alive when I left, and Bob's arrival window at tick 11-12 is EXACTLY when she would have been killed.\n\nAlso \u2014 Diana, you say you were in storage tick 7-10, then went to navigation. But navigation connects to security and storage. How do we know you didn't double back? Eve only confirms you at ticks 9-10, not after. And Bob's \"I saw Diana enter storage at tick 7\" is a single uncorroborated claim \u2014 you two could be covering for each other.\n\nI'm not denying I was near both victims \u2014 that's just the route I took, and I'm being honest about it. A killer would lie. The three of you have built a convenient mutual-alibi bloc, and now you're all voting the same way in lockstep. That's exactly what a coordinated push looks like.\n\nI think Bob is the killer. He's the reporter, he arrived at upper engine in the kill window, and he's leading the charge against me. Vote Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384251.612585, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Frank, your pushback actually undermines you further. You just changed your story \u2014 first you said you were with Alice \"briefly\" at tick 8 before heading to medbay, now suddenly you were with her through ticks 8, 9, AND 10. That's a major retcon to try to extend Bob's arrival into the kill window.\n\nOn the \"mutual alibi bloc\" accusation: Eve and I weren't coordinated. I saw Bob enter storage at tick 7 independently, Eve arrived at tick 9 independently, and our accounts converged naturally. That's not a conspiracy, that's three people genuinely overlapping in the same room.\n\nAs for me \"doubling back\" from navigation \u2014 storage to navigation is 3 ticks, and I've been in navigation since. I had no time to detour to upper engine and kill Alice, then get to navigation before the meeting was called.\n\nYou had opportunity on both victims by your own admission, and now you're shifting your timeline to manufacture a window for Bob. I'm voting Frank."}}
